        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A tank water heater is a corrosion countdown with a sacrificial rod buying time. Expect 8 to 12 years from gas and 10 to 15 from electric, know the date in your serial number, and treat any heater past 10 years as a planned replacement rather than a surprise.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If you are still inside that window, the anode rod and an annual flush are the cheapest years you will ever buy. If you are past it, use the quiet months to choose the replacement properly. Our <a href="/best-gas-water-heater/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-semibold hover:underline">best gas water heaters</a> guide is the place to start.
          </p>
